@competition @ai_agent @persona.platform_operator
Feature: Governed Factory Droid development workflow
  Factory Droid differentiates by packaging autonomous coding agents with
  enterprise control, readiness, and deployment options.

  Scenario: Platform operator rolls out Droid to a regulated engineering team
    Given a platform operator needs autonomous coding agents in a governed repository
    And the organization requires identity, model, command, and telemetry controls
    When the operator configures Droid for the project
    Then the organization can set model allow lists, tool policies, autonomy levels, and audit settings
    And developers can use Droid from the app, CLI, SDK, CI, or managed computers
    When Droid proposes or reviews code changes
    Then the operator can inspect usage, cost, productivity, and compliance signals
    And the team can improve repository readiness for more autonomous work

  Scenario: Developer continues work after hitting standard usage limits
    Given an individual developer is using Factory Droid for a long coding session
    When the developer reaches standard rolling usage limits
    Then Droid can offer lower-cost Droid Core model capacity or prepaid Extra Usage
    And the session can continue with a visible billing and capability tradeoff
